# CODEOWNERS — bkrupa/legacy-sports
#
# "Require review from Code Owners" is ENABLED in branch protection (T17, LS-3998).
# require_code_owner_review:true is set in .github/ruleset.json.
#
# Order matters: last matching pattern wins, so general rules come first,
# path-specific rules come last.
#
# The catch-all (*) assigns legacy-sports-review-bot as default owner for all
# files not covered by a more specific rule below (LS-5153, completing T3/LS-3860).
# This means the bot's APPROVE satisfies require_code_owner_review for normal code,
# and only the explicitly enumerated sensitive paths below require @bkrupa.
#
# All handles confirmed via LS-3859 (T2) — sole developer, no GitHub org teams.

# Default owner — review bot satisfies CODEOWNERS for all non-sensitive files
*                                 @legacy-sports-review-bot[bot]

# Workflows, CI config, and CI scripts
.github/workflows/**              @bkrupa
.github/actions/**                @bkrupa
.github/scripts/**                @bkrupa
.github/ruleset.json              @bkrupa
.github/CODEOWNERS                @bkrupa
.github/reviewer-rules.md         @bkrupa

# Infrastructure
terraform/**                      @bkrupa
scripts/apply-ruleset.sh          @bkrupa

# Auth / OAuth
lambdas/oauth-proxy/**            @bkrupa

# Payments (Stripe + Apple IAP)
lambdas/stripe-webhook/**         @bkrupa
lambdas/apple-iap/**              @bkrupa

# Database migrations
lib/db-client/migrations/**       @bkrupa

# Auth / authorization logic in the GraphQL lambda (security-sensitive subset only)
# The broad lambdas/db/** pattern previously required @bkrupa on every GraphQL
# resolver change; narrowed here so normal feature work falls through to the
# catch-all review-bot owner (LS-5153).
lambdas/db/src/schema/authorization*.ts   @bkrupa
lambdas/db/src/schema/entitlements.ts     @bkrupa

# CI design docs
docs/ci-cd/ci-greenfield-design.md         @bkrupa
docs/ci-cd/ci-greenfield-gap-analysis.md   @bkrupa
docs/ci-cd/ci-greenfield-copilot-evaluation.md @bkrupa
docs/ci-cd/archive/ci-bot-review-spec.md          @bkrupa
docs/ci-cd/archive/improved-ci-system-design.md   @bkrupa
